    "body": "Totally agree here - I brought this point up last year at the Knowledge Graph conference that good well written semantic HTML is the best data format for both human and machine-readable data.  [Back in 2012](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=4176236) it felt like there was an opportunity to bring Microformats and early Web Components together to make this possible, but a drive toward SPAs and API-driven applications killed it off.\r\n\r\nI'd like to see a move back to interoperable data using (X)HTML \r\n\r\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
